<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise in May month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise in May month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait rose to 12.043 billion dinars at the end of May, 1997 from 11.807 billion at the end April, the Central Bank said in a monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.106 billion dinars in May 1996.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					    May '97	     May '96</p>
<p> Cash					  51.0		 50.2</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	    26.4		 53.8</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	    1,788.4	    1,897.3</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		  2,694.0	    3,198.7</p>
<p> Other local investments		312.8		298.2</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			     3,600.4	    2,672.2</p>
<p> Foreign assets			 2,291.8	    2,041.0</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    735.8		412.8</p>
<p> Other assets			     542.7		481.9</p>
<p> Total				   12,043.2	   11,106.2</p>
<p>Note: Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.303 dinar)</p>
<p>- Ashraf Fouad, +965 240 8945</p>
</text>
